files-advanced-group-streaming = Progressive directory loading
files-advanced-group-enrichment = Background metadata probing
files-advanced-group-preview = Previews and thumbnails
files-advanced-group-io = Directory watching and file transfers
files-advanced-stream-delay = Progressive listing delay
files-advanced-stream-delay-help = Time elapsed before showing partial results for a slow directory scan (25–1000 ms).
files-advanced-stream-interval = Progressive refresh interval
files-advanced-stream-interval-help = Minimum interval between partial snapshot updates during a slow directory scan (50–2000 ms).
files-advanced-stream-min-entries = Minimum items for progressive listing
files-advanced-stream-min-entries-help = Minimum entries collected before showing partial results; set to 0 to disable progressive updates.
files-advanced-enrich-concurrency = Concurrent metadata batches
files-advanced-enrich-concurrency-help = Maximum background worker batches probing metadata per folder (1–16).
files-advanced-enrich-batch-size = Items per metadata batch
files-advanced-enrich-batch-size-help = Number of entries inspected in each background probing batch (8–256).
files-advanced-child-count-limit = Subfolder item count limit
files-advanced-child-count-limit-help = Maximum direct children counted per subfolder before displaying a lower bound (100–10000).
files-advanced-enrich-priority-limit = Viewport priority queue limit
files-advanced-enrich-priority-limit-help = Maximum visible items retained in priority order while scrolling rapidly (32–1024).
files-advanced-enrich-coalesce = Metadata flush coalescing window
files-advanced-enrich-coalesce-help = Coalescing delay before updating the view with routine metadata probes (8–250 ms).
files-advanced-enrich-reorder-coalesce = Reordering flush coalescing window
files-advanced-enrich-reorder-coalesce-help = Coalescing delay when metadata probes can change sorting or filter results (30–1000 ms).
files-advanced-enrich-max-updates = Maximum buffered updates per flush
files-advanced-enrich-max-updates-help = Maximum pending metadata updates buffered before forcing an immediate UI flush (64–4096).
files-advanced-preview-workers = Preview worker concurrency
files-advanced-preview-workers-help = Concurrent background workers generating previews and thumbnails (1–8).
files-advanced-preview-cache-entries = Preview cache entry limit
files-advanced-preview-cache-entries-help = Maximum number of decoded thumbnails and metadata snapshots kept in memory (32–2048).
files-advanced-preview-cache-mib = Preview cache memory limit
files-advanced-preview-cache-mib-help = Memory budget for decoded preview thumbnails across the window (16–1024 MiB).
files-advanced-thumbnail-source-mib = Thumbnail source size limit
files-advanced-thumbnail-source-mib-help = Maximum source file size decoded for image and audio artwork thumbnails (4–256 MiB).
files-advanced-video-timeout = Video thumbnail timeout
files-advanced-video-timeout-help = Timeout for extracting a preview frame from video files with FFmpeg (2–60 s).
files-advanced-watch-debounce = Directory watch debounce
files-advanced-watch-debounce-help = Delay before reconciling filesystem change notifications into the active view (25–1000 ms).
files-advanced-watch-limit = Incremental watch path limit
files-advanced-watch-limit-help = Maximum changed paths applied incrementally before falling back to a full folder rescan (32–2048).
files-advanced-local-buffer = Local copy buffer size
files-advanced-local-buffer-help = Buffer size used when reading and writing local files during copies and cross-device moves (16–1024 KiB).
files-advanced-remote-buffer = Remote transfer buffer size
files-advanced-remote-buffer-help = Stream buffer size used when transferring files between local storage and remote servers (16–1024 KiB).
